// ch11 (round 2, R2-2 / #2227): the .vibex rows of the require-pin lane
// table. Round 2 measured the same pin p31 carries answering differently
// once the file was a .vibex: run/compile said `unknown # directive:
// pkg` (the script-head directive scan read the pin's `#pkg:sha1:` as a
// `#` directive) and check said `unexpected token: =`. #2227's fix
// blanks the pin before the .vibex entry validation and before check's
// pre-parse, so every lane now agrees with the .vibe build lane: the
// probe compiles and runs (prints below), and both directives answer
// clean (exit 0).
//! cli: run
//! cli: check
require @vibe/core 0.2.0 = #pkg:sha1:0000000000000000000000000000000000000000

fn main with Console {
  println("pin head parsed")
}
